# Kanban Review QA and Done lessons

Applies when working on any card under `.devtool/features/` during **Review** or when the user closes a card.

Full workflow: [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § User-reported QA fixes, § Card Done — lessons learned.

## User-reported QA fixes (mandatory)

When the user reports a **Review** issue and you fix it:

| Card `labels` | Append dated record under |
| ------------- | ------------------------- |
| `bug` | **`## Corrective Action`** |
| feature (default), `agent` | **`## Decisions`** |

Format: `**QA follow-up (YYYY-MM-DD):**` symptom → fix → test/doc pointer. When paths or symbols changed, note **Labels:** appended paths/methods (or `none` if card already complete).

**Same turn — refresh card scope** (mandatory when the fix changes code):

1. **`## Feature Areas`** — append product-area label(s) when fix crosses into an area not listed (`python scripts/resolve_feature_areas.py --list`).
2. **`## Label Paths`** — append edited/added file paths not already on the card (dedupe).
3. **`## Label Methods`** — append `path` — `symbol` bullets for new handlers, helpers, or tests touched.
4. **`docs/feature-areas.yaml`** — when new paths/handlers are durable for that area (same gate as initial implementation).

- Bump card `modified` in the **same turn** as the fix.
- Do **not** rely on chat history as the only record.

## Do not

- Skip card **QA follow-up** recording because the fix was small
- Skip **Label Paths** / **Label Methods** refresh when the fix edited files or symbols not on the card
- Remove user **Feature Areas** labels — append only

## Card Done — lessons learned (mandatory)

When the user says the card is **done** / **closed** / ready for **Done**:

1. Read the card (including all **QA follow-up** bullets).
2. Update **≥1 skill** + **≥1 rule** (different learnings) + relevant **`docs/`** / registry / `feature-areas.yaml`.
3. Add **`## Lessons captured (YYYY-MM-DD)`** on the card listing updated paths.

**User** moves `review` → `done/` — agents capture lessons, not column moves.

## Do not

- Put pytest-only checklist items in **`## QA Review`** (agent workflow — see kanban-markdown § QA Review)
- Skip **lessons captured** when user says Done because AC were already `[x]`
